.TH WEBRUNNER 1 "May 2026" "webrunner 0.8.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
webrunner \- zero-config development web server with CGI and .htaccess support
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B webrunner
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ ROOT ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B webrunner
is a single-binary Rust development web server. Point it at a directory and
you get static files, directory listings, classic CGI scripts (Perl, PHP,
TypeScript/JavaScript via
.BR bun ),
URL rewriting, basic auth, custom error pages, and self-signed HTTPS \(em
all driven by familiar Apache-style
.B .htaccess
files.

Built for local development and quick prototyping. Not a production server.

The
.I ROOT
positional argument selects the document root; it is equivalent to
.BR --root .
The default is the current working directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI -p\fR,\fP\ --port " PORT"
HTTP port. Default
.BR 8080 .
.TP
.B --https
Enable HTTPS. Auto-generates a self-signed certificate cached in
.BR ~/.config/webrunner/
on first run.
.TP
.BI --https-port " PORT"
HTTPS port. Default
.BR 8443 .
.TP
.BI --cert " PATH"
Path to TLS certificate (PEM). Requires
.BR --key .
Implies
.BR --https .
.TP
.BI --key " PATH"
Path to TLS private key (PEM). Requires
.BR --cert .
.TP
.B --no-index
Disable directory listings; return 403 for directory requests that have no
matching
.BR DirectoryIndex .
.TP
.BI --root " DIR"
Document root. Also accepted as a positional argument. Path is canonicalised
at startup.
.TP
.BI --bind " ADDR"
Bind address(es). Accepts IPv4 and IPv6 literals; comma-separated and
repeatable. Default
.BR 0.0.0.0,:: .
.TP
.BI --cgi " EXT[,EXT...]"
Extra extensions to execute as CGI. The
.B pl
and
.B php
extensions are always CGI; this flag enables
.B js
and
.B ts
via
.BR bun .
.TP
.BI --no-cgi " EXT[,EXT...]"
Disable always-on CGI for the listed extensions
.RB ( pl ,
.BR php ).
Mutually exclusive with
.B --cgi
on the same extension.
.TP
.BI --cgi-timeout " SECS"
CGI script timeout in seconds. Default
.BR 30 .
A value of
.B 0
disables the limit.
.TP
.BI --log-level " LEVEL"
Verbosity:
.BR off ,
.BR warn ,
.BR info ,
.BR debug .
Default
.BR info .
.B debug
surfaces recognized-but-unsupported
.B .htaccess
directives.
.TP
.BI --log " PATH"
Access log file path. Use
.B -
for stdout. Combined Log Format, one line per request.
.TP
.BI --compression " ON|OFF"
Brotli / gzip compression for text-shaped static responses. Default
.BR on .
Applies to
.BR text/* ,
.BR application/json ,
.BR application/javascript ,
.BR image/svg+xml ,
.BR application/wasm .
Responses under 256 bytes and
.B Range
requests are served uncompressed.
.TP
.BI --hsts " SECS"
Send
.B Strict-Transport-Security
on HTTPS responses with this
.BR max-age .
Default: header not sent.
.TP
.B --hsts-include-subdomains
Add the
.B includeSubDomains
directive to the HSTS header. Requires
.BR --hsts .
.TP
.B --hsts-preload
Add the
.B preload
directive to the HSTS header. Requires
.BR --hsts .
.TP
.B --examples
Print a rich, colorized usage cookbook and exit.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.B -V, --version
Show version and exit.
.SH ".HTACCESS"
A practical subset of Apache's
.B .htaccess
is supported. Deeper files override shallower ones; unknown directives are
skipped with a warning on stderr (use
.B --log-level debug
to see recognized-but-unsupported entries).

Supported directives:
.IP \[bu] 2
.B DirectoryIndex
\(em comma-separated index file list.
.IP \[bu]
.B Options
.RB \(+- Indexes
\(em toggle directory listings.
.IP \[bu]
.B ErrorDocument
\(em custom error pages by status code.
.IP \[bu]
.BR AddType ,
.B AddDefaultCharset
\(em MIME-type overrides.
.IP \[bu]
.B Redirect
(301 / 302) and
.B RedirectMatch
(regex with capture substitution; status-only forms for 204 / 4xx).
.IP \[bu]
.BR RewriteEngine ,
.BR RewriteRule ,
.BR RewriteCond ,
.B RewriteBase
\(em URL rewriting. Flags:
.BR [QSA] ,
.BR [L] ,
.BR [R] ,
.BR [NC] ,
.BR [F] ,
.BR [G] .
.IP \[bu]
.B AuthType Basic
with
.BR .htpasswd
files supporting bcrypt
.RB ( $2y$\(rs ),
SHA-1
.RB ( {SHA}\(rs ),
and Apache MD5
.RB ( $apr1$\(rs ).
Authorization via
.BR "Require valid-user" ,
.BR "Require user <name>" ,
.BR "Require ip <CIDR>" ,
.BR "Require not ip <CIDR>" .
.IP \[bu]
.BR Allow ,
.BR Deny ,
.B Order
\(em legacy Apache 2.2 IP-based access control.
.IP \[bu]
.BR Header
(set / setifempty / add / append / merge / unset / echo / edit / edit*) with
.B always|onsuccess
conditions and placeholders
.RB ( %t ,
.BR %D ,
.BR %l ,
.BR %s ,
.BR %H ,
.BR %m ,
.BR %U ).
.IP \[bu]
.BR ExpiresActive ,
.BR ExpiresDefault ,
.B ExpiresByType
\(em
.BR Cache-Control
and
.B Expires
headers per response MIME type. Time-spec:
.BR "access plus N <unit>" .
.IP \[bu]
.B <IfModule>
blocks pass through (their contents always apply).
.B <FilesMatch "regex">
and
.B <Files "glob">
scope contained
.BR Header ,
.BR RewriteRule ,
auth, and
.B AddType
directives to files whose basename matches the pattern.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/webrunner/cert.pem
Self-signed certificate cached on first
.B --https
run.
.TP
.B ~/.config/webrunner/key.pem
Matching private key.
.TP
.B .htaccess
Per-directory configuration file; merged from document root down to the
target directory.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Clean shutdown after
.B Ctrl+C
or
.BR SIGTERM .
.TP
.B 1
Startup error (bad arguments, port already in use, missing certificate
file, etc.). Errors are reported to stderr.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Serve the current directory on
.BR http://localhost:8080 :
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
webrunner
.EE
.in
.PP
HTTPS on
.B :8443
with a self-signed certificate cached for next time:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
webrunner --https
.EE
.in
.PP
Restrict to loopback and write an access log:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
webrunner --bind 127.0.0.1,::1 --log /var/log/webrunner.access.log
.EE
.in
.PP
Run
.B "webrunner --examples"
for a full colorized cookbook.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR htpasswd (1),
.BR apache2 (8),
the project README for the full feature list and the supported
.B .htaccess
directive table.
